            <ArticleTitle>The V-stent: a novel technique for coronary bifurcation stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>320-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intracoronary stenting as a transcatheter treatment for bifurcation stenoses remains controversial. A novel technique of coronary bifurcation stenting is reported. A 15 mm Palmaz-Schatz stent is bent 180 degrees at its bridge articulation into a V- configuration and mounted on two balloon-catheters linked together by adhesive tape. This unified stent delivery system was used successfully in five cases of porcine coronary bifurcation stenting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
